# Phaser rendering

- Scenes render read models/events and emit semantic input; they do not own game rules.
- Use WebGL-first configuration and nearest-neighbor pixel rendering.
- Dispose scene listeners, timers, textures created solely by the scene, and pooled objects.
- Use normal interactive objects for selection, heroes, markers, and order controls.
- Use `SpriteGPULayer` only for compatible single-texture populations and batch updates; preallocate where appropriate.
- Do not assign physics to every rank-and-file sprite.
- Cull labels, effects, and icons by camera bounds and zoom.
- Keep camera/presentation interpolation non-authoritative.
- Add a diagnostic scene or benchmark for scale-sensitive renderer changes.
- Maintain a reduced visual-density setting.
